{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "plumbing_ageing",
  "spec": ["plumbing 6.7", "plumbing 7.3", "plumbing 10.1", "plumbing 14.22"],
  "description": "Test 22 (pollution 4.9.3 rule, shipped curves, hand-derived): a pump of 1000 at (10,10) with ageing rate k = 1, its own pipe, a consumer of 500 at (12,10). A month sets the ageing flag; the pass then writes water used 500 (ratio 0.5) and at state 8 ages the producer: usage = 500 / 1000 = 0.5, condition 0 + 0.45 (usage curve) x 1 (funding curve at 1.0) x 1 = 0.45, and clears the flag (a pass without a month leaves 0.45). Unpowered: production 0 and water used 0 -> usage 0 (both must be > 0) -> + 0.1 -> 0.55. The funding input is the department's funding fraction: at 1.2 the funding curve gives 0.9 -> + 0.1 x 0.9 = 0.64. Condition 99 with the default thresholds 99 / 99 -> 99.1 >= t2 -> lot.SetCondition(4); thresholds 50 / 200 and condition 60 -> 60.1 >= t1 -> SetCondition(2); condition 10 -> nothing. FindWaterBuildings: the producer the department funds locally at 0.8 is the lowest funded (strict <, from 2.0); the worst condition ratio is 10.1 / max(50, 200) = 0.0505 -> pct trunc(5.05) = 5; a producer with condition 0 never beats the start value 0.",
  "steps": [
    {"op": "plumbing_env", "water": [[11, 10]]},
    {"op": "plumbing_create"},
    {"op": "plumbing_init"},
    {"op": "plumbing_message", "type": "ConnectionsReady"},
